# Reader Flutter — platform contract

App: `apps/reader_flutter/`. Targets: iOS, Android, Web, macOS, Linux, Windows.

Folder roles live in `apps/reader_flutter/lib/CLAUDE.md`. Follow that file for paths; this rule is the contract.

## Where code goes

| Kind | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Logic, tokens, l10n, storage, security | root `lib/` (`config`, `design`, `l10n`, `models`, `providers`, `router`, `storage`, `security`, `utils`) |
| Route adapters | `lib/screens/` — branch only |
| iOS + Android UI | `lib/mobile/` |
| Web UI | `lib/web/` |
| macOS + Linux + Windows UI | `lib/desktop/` |

`lib/widgets/` is legacy mobile UI. New mobile UI goes in `lib/mobile/`. Move a legacy file there when you edit it.

## Rules

1. Data, auth, sync, and business rules have one implementation in common.
2. UI is implemented separately in `mobile/`, `web/`, and `desktop/`. Those three folders do not import each other. Only `lib/screens/` may import all three.
3. Share `AppColors`, `AppSpace`, `AppRadius`, and `AppTheme`. Keep widget trees and scaffolds in the platform folder that owns them.
4. Ship the same user-facing behavior on all six targets unless the task scopes one platform.
5. Add every user-visible string to both `lib/l10n/app_en.arb` and `app_am.arb`.

## Route adapter

Branch web, then desktop. Mobile is the unguarded fallthrough. Narrow web (under 720px) uses the mobile UI. `useDesktopShell` is false on web.

```dart
if (useWebShell(context)) {
  return const WebPageScaffold(body: HomeScreenBody());
}
if (useDesktopShell(context)) {
  return const DesktopPageScaffold(body: DesktopHomeScreenBody());
}
return const MobileHomeScreen();
```

Verify with `make reader-run-{android,ios,web,macos,linux,windows}`.
